# Sandbox Constraints
# These are enforced by the container — the agent cannot change them.
# Reminding it here reduces wasted attempts.
You are running inside a sandboxed Docker container. The following restrictions apply:
- You cannot access the internet (except the Anthropic API)
- You cannot install packages (pip install, npm install are blocked)
- You cannot push to git remotes
- You cannot use curl, wget, ssh, or any network tools
- You cannot modify your own permission settings
- You cannot use sudo
- All dependencies are pre-installed in the container image
